{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion","id":1560926,"title":"Demon The Fallen Lores Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-23T23:50:58-07:00","id":1560926,"title":"Demon The Fallen Lores Discussion","content":"<br /> So I've always liked Demon the Fallen. Discovering it and the rest of White Wolf games is what got me into ttrpgs beyond dnd. I love these games(especially cofd) their settings, and how game mechanics melded, informed, and drove the stories of its characters.<br /> <br /> However I've haven't been satisfied with how the powers of dtf work and function, mechanically or narratively. So I wanted to do something about that and figure out or make an alternative for myself.<br /> <br /> I myself have never actually gotten the opportunity to play the games, this is more for my, I guess fan-fiction work relating to demon. But as I said before I've always liked the melding of mechanics and narrative, so I want to create a power framework for my, pcs/docs to use.<br /> <br /> Starting off, I liked how v5 consolidated the disciplines and demon does posses a few, in my opinion redundant lores, so this my attempt to consolidate them myself.<br /> <br /> Awakening, Celestials, Death, Firmament, Forge, Flesh, Fundament, Longing, Patterns, Paths, Radiance, Spirits, Wild, and Humanity<br /> <br /> Flesh-Incorporates Transfiguration, Deal with direct manipulation of the organic body.<br /> Fundament-Consolidate all the elemental lores(Flame, Winds, Earth, Light, and Storms) and any other mundane force in the material world.<br /> Paths-Incorporates Portals and Realms. Dealing with all forms of travel and transit.<br /> Wild-Incorporates Beasts, Deals with all the other living things.<br /> <br /> Humanity-Communication &amp; Commin Lore, Longing-Inspiration &amp; Emotions, Radiance-Command &amp; Exaltation<br /> <br /> Devils<br /> Celestials, Fundament, Radiance<br /> <br /> Scourges<br /> Awakening, Firmament, Fundament<br /> <br /> Malefactors<br /> Forge, Fundament, Paths<br /> <br /> Fiends<br /> Firmament, Patterns, Paths<br /> <br /> Defilers<br /> Flesh, Fundament, Longing<br /> <br /> Devourers<br /> Awakening, Flesh, Wild<br /> <br /> Slayers<br /> Death, Paths. Spirits<br /> <br /> Common Lore<br /> Humanity<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T18:10:35-07:00","id":1560953,"title":"","content":"I think squeezing all of the elemental Lores into a single Lore is a bit much, especially when it's not a Common Lore here like Humanity is. I think what you could do is have Earth and MAYBE Flame folded into Fundament (since it represents the Earth we live on), and then put Winds and Storms into Firmament (which refers to the Heavens.) Light can be added to Celestials if you really want to place it somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T18:53:40-07:00","id":1561013,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> While the notion of &quot;elements are Fundament&quot; is intuitive, it is from an Alchemical perspective that doesn't really fit Demon.<br /> <br /> Their idea of &quot;constituent elements of reality&quot; is the whole Lore package, they're agnostic on matter theory, those Lores don't really work together as building blocks for something, and this affects the spread of their powers.<br /> <br /> Demon work from the perspective of the Houses. The taxonomy of Lores must be tied to what each House represents and their realm of dominion, the tasks they're made to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T11:17:28-07:00","id":1561032,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I read the Core. I forgot how central some of the elemental lores were to the houses.<br /> <br /> How about something like this<br /> <br /> Flame, Earth, Winds*, and Storms*<br /> *They both have overlap at their higher levels, that I'm not sure how to deal with.<br /> <br /> Firmament incorporates the classic powers of the Fundament(Adhesion, Gravity, Inertia, etc.) and its own classic powers over connections(Remote Viewing, Scry, etc.)<br /> -I always found it odd with it being stated that the Neberu setted up the gravitational orbits and other subtle aspects of reality, instead had the Lore of Light as their in-house lore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T11:47:13-07:00","id":1561060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrere Oil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561032#post1561032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while since I read the Core. I forgot how central some of the elemental lores were to the houses.<br /> <br /> How about something like this<br /> <br /> Flame, Earth, Winds*, and Storms*<br /> *They both have overlap at their higher levels, that I'm not sure how to deal with.<br /> <br /> Firmament incorporates the classic powers of the Fundament(Adhesion, Gravity, Inertia, etc.) and its own classic powers over connections(Remote Viewing, Scry, etc.)<br /> -I always found it odd with it being stated that the Neberu setted up the gravitational orbits and other subtle aspects of reality, instead had the Lore of Light as their in-house lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you first need a plan, a clearer idea of what you think the problem is and how you think the result should be.<br /> <br /> Just moving powers through Lores will just make a messy system even worse as you don't have a picture of what you need, what the system may lack, what may be excess, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Lores have some thematic coherence. They're built for the distribution of powers, give or take things like Neberu without Gravity. They were built with a plan of the themes of each House and how the needed powers and domains would be distributed, along with which archetypes for Demons would be reinforced by the game.<br /> <br /> Sit down and think what kind of picture you want before you move pieces around to find out what broke only afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T11:14:47-07:00","id":1561609,"title":"","content":"Me personally, I prefer to use the system from &quot;Dark Ages: Devil's Due&quot; when I run Demon. They just feel more uniquely demonic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T21:19:33-07:00","id":1561646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561609#post1561609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me personally, I prefer to use the system from &quot;Dark Ages: Devil's Due&quot; when I run Demon. They just feel more uniquely demonic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the exact problem.<br /> <br /> First, Devil's Due, while kind of DtF DA, is before all else a Vampire supplement with a structure of powers that is good and balanced against the Vampire setting and themes, but gives no solid framework for a new game, with its own themes and questions.<br /> <br /> Second, it's limited in scope and vision, reduce itself to explore the narrow notion of demons as servants of evil in the simplest sense, not its own literary work but subservient to a morality play within Vampire.<br /> <br /> Good if all you want to do is to play the spirits the Vampire infernalists deal with, but limited to say the list if you want to play full spectrum the concept of a creator godling wronged by Creation in the past and now coming to terms with war trauma, broken ideologies, corruption of your labor's fruits and the question of where to go from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T08:44:20-07:00","id":1561652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561646#post1561646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the exact problem.<br /> <br /> First, Devil's Due, while kind of DtF DA, is before all else a Vampire supplement with a structure of powers that is good and balanced against the Vampire setting and themes, but gives no solid framework for a new game, with its own themes and questions.<br /> <br /> Second, it's limited in scope and vision, reduce itself to explore the narrow notion of demons as servants of evil in the simplest sense, not its own literary work but subservient to a morality play within Vampire.<br /> <br /> Good if all you want to do is to play the spirits the Vampire infernalists deal with, but limited to say the list if you want to play full spectrum the concept of a creator godling wronged by Creation in the past and now coming to terms with war trauma, broken ideologies, corruption of your labor's fruits and the question of where to go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of completely disagree. The very fact that your Torment rating determines access to power in Devil's Due does a lot more to work themes into the mechanics than core D:tF does. To me, core D:tF feels grossly derivative of Vampire and Werewolf and Changeling in terms of mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T15:21:57-07:00","id":1561662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561652#post1561652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of completely disagree. The very fact that your Torment rating determines access to power in Devil's Due does a lot more to work themes into the mechanics than core D:tF does. To me, core D:tF feels grossly derivative of Vampire and Werewolf and Changeling in terms of mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does Torment determining access to power does more to work themes into mechanics? And which themes?<br /> <br /> As for being grossly derivative, while I don't completely disagree, I don't see it as being so much so, and in fact I'm not sure if lumping Vampire, Werewolf and Changeling makes for a compelling argument that it is derivative, no more than any other gameline.<br /> <br /> My argument wasn't that the rules of Devil's Due do not work in themes. My argument was that it doesn't cover the themes a complete new gameline need. You didn't addressed this.<br /> <br /> The rule of Torment risking to change how your powers manifest, for example, I think it's a very good idea. Needs polishing, but is coherent with the narrative of the psychological weight of the war and is not something we saw before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T16:08:10-07:00","id":1561663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561662#post1561662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does Torment determining access to power does more to work themes into mechanics? And which themes?<br /> <br /> As for being grossly derivative, while I don't completely disagree, I don't see it as being so much so, and in fact I'm not sure if lumping Vampire, Werewolf and Changeling makes for a compelling argument that it is derivative, no more than any other gameline.<br /> <br /> My argument wasn't that the rules of Devil's Due do not work in themes. My argument was that it doesn't cover the themes a complete new gameline need. You didn't addressed this.<br /> <br /> The rule of Torment risking to change how your powers manifest, for example, I think it's a very good idea. Needs polishing, but is coherent with the narrative of the psychological weight of the war and is not something we saw before.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of temptation to evil. If demons power levels are determined by how evil they are, then choosing to be good carries a lot more weight. <br /> <br /> I do think Devil's Due covers the themes a complete game line needs. For example, it already has a similar mechanic to the one you just brought up, with the appearance of your Apocalypstic Form and the mechanical effect it has changing based on your Torment Score.<br /> <br /> I guess my question to you is this: What does D:tF core have that Devil's Due lacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T19:10:38-07:00","id":1561671,"title":"","content":"A Hazy yet Awe-Inspiring Past that has left Remnants across the world. A need to erect webs and networks of Pacts and Thralls. Lack of a settled shared society, full of rivalries and potential conflicts. Balancing all the above with living a mortal life in a world wholly different from what they can remember. The struggle between Damnation and Redemption and how it should even be defined, followed through, or whether it even really exists.<br /> <br /> Those are the ideas and concepts I associate with Demon The Fallen, even if it isn't able to piece them together in a satisfactory way I and and probably many others feel.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Torment risking. I feel the temptation to dip/fall into Torment is something DtF lacks. I also feel like that, since cruel/sadistic actions already incur Torment, many of the High-Torment effects should be things that the fallen could always do before the fall.<br /> <br /> Another thing I thought about, connecting to what I said earlier about the struggle to define Damnation/Redemption, is to question the idea/use of Torment. Sometimes awful things must be genuinely done, for the good of others or oneself. I'm thinking of the philosophy of the Devil-Tigers, who seek to become righteous heavenly demons and reform the Thousand Hells and how one of the Fallen might react to that idea and possibly adapt for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T06:15:46-07:00","id":1561677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561663#post1561663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The theme of temptation to evil. If demons power levels are determined by how evil they are, then choosing to be good carries a lot more weight.<br /> <br /> I do think Devil's Due covers the themes a complete game line needs. For example, it already has a similar mechanic to the one you just brought up, with the appearance of your Apocalypstic Form and the mechanical effect it has changing based on your Torment Score.<br /> <br /> I guess my question to you is this: What does D:tF core have that Devil's Due lacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temptation to Evil is a Vampire theme, and the form seen in Devil's Due is particularly good for Dark Ages. I don't think linking power directly to Torment is the best way to make for nuance in play.<br /> <br /> I'll state again some of the themes I see in DtF and not in Devil's Due. If you don't care about them, that's fine, but is a weakness for Devil's Due nonetheless. If you think Devil's Due does a good job addressing them, I'm interested in the argument:<br /> <br /> 1.<b> A godling wronged by Creation</b>. The demon as a minor creator deity that faced undue harm as &quot;compensation&quot;. Evil is tangential, not core.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Dealing with war trauma</b>. DtF's Torment isn't about malice, it's about how war changes you when returning to a civilian life.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Shattered ideals and lost innocence</b>. In DtF your character's past as an Angel isn't simply a background, but a present matter. You're given the opportunity to try and rebuild, what do you make of it?<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Your work, corrupted</b>. DtF reminds you all the time that you built this world, and what you see is how your creation was put to use by others.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Memory of making History</b>. Memory is ever a theme in DtF, but it has the distinct flavor of the glorious past that shaped the present. Around you is a world shaped by the feats of your time.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Rebuilding life and society</b>. You're a prisoner released with others, a survivor of the end of your old world, you're starting a new life where nothing will be the same as before.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>How to define Redemption</b>. VtM question if redemption is possible when it is unknowable. DtF question what you do when you're the only authority on what redemption even is.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Faith as Responsibility</b>. What inspiring faith in others implies for you and what you owe them back? How do you cultivate them, and in which direction?<br /> <br /> 9. <b>Overall how you choose to change the lives you touch</b>. Vampires have no choice in being predators. Demons define themselves by being important to others, be it cultists, Thralls, or the loved ones and work colleagues of their host.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Judge yourself and the world</b>. DtF doesn't place you under the scrutiny of another force or entity. Even your fellows are divided. With all its downsides, Torment isn't intrinsically wrong. You're invited to be the one to settle good and evil, sin and punishment.<br /> <br /> I personally don't see Devil's Due working well in any of those, and sometimes even going against it. The need to be high Torment to get full access to your powers is specially bad for my view of those themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T12:14:07-07:00","id":1561690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561677#post1561677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temptation to Evil is a Vampire theme, and the form seen in Devil's Due is particularly good for Dark Ages. I don't think linking power directly to Torment is the best way to make for nuance in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a vampire theme, sure. But not only should it also be a Demom theme, I think it has to be in order to make some of the other themes you mentioned work. Defining redemption as a theme doesn't carry much weight if being good is the easy option, redemption and temptation are intrinsically linked concepts. Being good and redeeming yourself is hard because doing bad things you need to be redeemed for is so easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561677#post1561677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll state again some of the themes I see in DtF and not in Devil's Due. If you don't care about them, that's fine, but is a weakness for Devil's Due nonetheless. If you think Devil's Due does a good job addressing them, I'm interested in the argument:<br /> <br /> 1.<b> A godling wronged by Creation</b>. The demon as a minor creator deity that faced undue harm as &quot;compensation&quot;. Evil is tangential, not core.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Dealing with war trauma</b>. DtF's Torment isn't about malice, it's about how war changes you when returning to a civilian life.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Shattered ideals and lost innocence</b>. In DtF your character's past as an Angel isn't simply a background, but a present matter. You're given the opportunity to try and rebuild, what do you make of it?<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Your work, corrupted</b>. DtF reminds you all the time that you built this world, and what you see is how your creation was put to use by others.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Memory of making History</b>. Memory is ever a theme in DtF, but it has the distinct flavor of the glorious past that shaped the present. Around you is a world shaped by the feats of your time.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Rebuilding life and society</b>. You're a prisoner released with others, a survivor of the end of your old world, you're starting a new life where nothing will be the same as before.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>How to define Redemption</b>. VtM question if redemption is possible when it is unknowable. DtF question what you do when you're the only authority on what redemption even is.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Faith as Responsibility</b>. What inspiring faith in others implies for you and what you owe them back? How do you cultivate them, and in which direction?<br /> <br /> 9. <b>Overall how you choose to change the lives you touch</b>. Vampires have no choice in being predators. Demons define themselves by being important to others, be it cultists, Thralls, or the loved ones and work colleagues of their host.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Judge yourself and the world</b>. DtF doesn't place you under the scrutiny of another force or entity. Even your fellows are divided. With all its downsides, Torment isn't intrinsically wrong. You're invited to be the one to settle good and evil, sin and punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't deny those are themes in D:tF. My question to you is, what makes the D:tF Lore system better suited for embodying those ideas than the Devils Due Arcana system?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561677#post1561677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't see Devil's Due working well in any of those, and sometimes even going against it. The need to be high Torment to get full access to your powers is specially bad for my view of those themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T12:16:08-07:00","id":1561691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrere Oil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561671#post1561671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hazy yet Awe-Inspiring Past that has left Remnants across the world. A need to erect webs and networks of Pacts and Thralls. Lack of a settled shared society, full of rivalries and potential conflicts. Balancing all the above with living a mortal life in a world wholly different from what they can remember. The struggle between Damnation and Redemption and how it should even be defined, followed through, or whether it even really exists.<br /> <br /> Those are the ideas and concepts I associate with Demon The Fallen, even if it isn't able to piece them together in a satisfactory way I and and probably many others feel.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Torment risking. I feel the temptation to dip/fall into Torment is something DtF lacks. I also feel like that, since cruel/sadistic actions already incur Torment, many of the High-Torment effects should be things that the fallen could always do before the fall.<br /> <br /> Another thing I thought about, connecting to what I said earlier about the struggle to define Damnation/Redemption, is to question the idea/use of Torment. Sometimes awful things must be genuinely done, for the good of others or oneself. I'm thinking of the philosophy of the Devil-Tigers, who seek to become righteous heavenly demons and reform the Thousand Hells and how one of the Fallen might react to that idea and possibly adapt for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree those are themes in D:tF. I'm just saying that I think the power system from Devil's Due works just as well at embodying those themes, while also just feeling more demonic in nature. Playing an altruistic demon who is genuinely focused on redemption and healing the world is a HUGE character choice in Devil's Due in a way it just isn't in Fallen, and I think that works a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T02:29:24-07:00","id":1561701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561690#post1561690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. A godling wronged by Creation.<br /> <br /> I said evil is tangential, not core. Power derived from Torment doubles down on the idea of the character as a manifestation of Evil rather as a creator deity.<br /> <br /> 2. Dealing with war trauma.<br /> <br /> Torment as trauma leads the character to turn everything into a weapon. Torment as a source of power is something else entirely.<br /> <br /> 3. Shattered ideals and lost innocence.<br /> <br /> Devil's Due has nothing to enforce this theme, especially the possibility of rebuilding or build something new.<br /> <br /> Vice as a trait also focus too much on evil and corruption as defining the demon rather than being a state they can outgrow.<br /> <br /> 4. Your work, corrupted.<br /> <br /> Lores as a system have the potential to cover a greater range of feats than buying a number of fixed effects, and tie those to the notion of you having knowledge and access to the building blocks of Creation.<br /> <br /> This actualize in play the idea of participation in said creation, and together with Memory the notion that you had a plan or expectation for your part in it, and reality fell short.<br /> <br /> No one here is arguing that DtF's Lores as they were done managed it, but Devil's Due proposal ditches the effort entirely.<br /> <br /> 5. Memory of making History.<br /> <br /> Mostly I didn't see in it mechanics to remember the world before and bring it in play. I may have missed something.<br /> <br /> 6. Rebuilding life and society.<br /> <br /> DtF has an actual society of demons forming. It is badly defined, but that's the point: a bunch of fugitives/survivors/refugees with memories of a destroyed past trying to build present from scratch.<br /> <br /> 7. How to define Redemption.<br /> <br /> You didn't got the theme at all. Demon isn't in it to ask if you redeem yourself according to any particular standard of redemption.<br /> <br /> It asks which standards you build. What counts as redemption, what must be done or suffered to fit the bill and clean the record.<br /> <br /> Not just for you, by the way.<br /> <br /> 8. Faith as Responsibility.<br /> <br /> Devil's Due default to Thralls and cultists as the medieval idea of Devil worshippers. They get a Torment trait as they're corrupted by you and what empowers the Pact is their decision to go ahead.<br /> <br /> In DtF the Pact is defined by faith, by intimate, confident belief in the power of a covenant, but without fixing the nature of this covenant. You define how you go for it, what you'll be for your Thrall and how you'll fit or subvert expectations and guide their future outside giving orders.<br /> <br /> 9. Overall how you choose to change the lives you touch.<br /> <br /> DtF doesn't prescribe what your powers or your presence do to people. You have potential in as many directions as possible. You're not Evil by nature, your &quot;nature&quot; is a blank slate.<br /> <br /> Your choice isn't a binary of letting Torment go forth or block it, it's an open question of which paths you see and what you choose to make of them.<br /> <br /> 10. Judge yourself and the world.<br /> <br /> Again, you're not seeking redemption unless you want. You're not at fault to begin with. You are passing judgment and all the standards are up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall DtF needs revisions, no one denied that, but it has the basic structure and narrative in a good direction. It's also open for interpretation and exploration.<br /> <br /> Your main point is the very problem with Devil's Due in all of this: feeling more &quot;demonic&quot;. This is subjective as fuck and thematically narrow. Devil's Due don't invite you to explore what you think a Fallen is or can be, it assumes a given notion of &quot;demon&quot; and roll with it, love it or leave it.<br /> <br /> It subordinates all the questions above to this conceptualization of what a demon is instead of making it one option among many, while DtF works to ask you how you conceptualize Fallen Angels and what you'll do from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T06:24:36-07:00","id":1561706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561701#post1561701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. A godling wronged by Creation.<br /> <br /> I said evil is tangential, not core. Power derived from Torment doubles down on the idea of the character as a manifestation of Evil rather as a creator deity.<br /> <br /> 2. Dealing with war trauma.<br /> <br /> Torment as trauma leads the character to turn everything into a weapon. Torment as a source of power is something else entirely.<br /> <br /> 3. Shattered ideals and lost innocence.<br /> <br /> Devil's Due has nothing to enforce this theme, especially the possibility of rebuilding or build something new.<br /> <br /> Vice as a trait also focus too much on evil and corruption as defining the demon rather than being a state they can outgrow.<br /> <br /> 4. Your work, corrupted.<br /> <br /> Lores as a system have the potential to cover a greater range of feats than buying a number of fixed effects, and tie those to the notion of you having knowledge and access to the building blocks of Creation.<br /> <br /> This actualize in play the idea of participation in said creation, and together with Memory the notion that you had a plan or expectation for your part in it, and reality fell short.<br /> <br /> No one here is arguing that DtF's Lores as they were done managed it, but Devil's Due proposal ditches the effort entirely.<br /> <br /> 5. Memory of making History.<br /> <br /> Mostly I didn't see in it mechanics to remember the world before and bring it in play. I may have missed something.<br /> <br /> 6. Rebuilding life and society.<br /> <br /> DtF has an actual society of demons forming. It is badly defined, but that's the point: a bunch of fugitives/survivors/refugees with memories of a destroyed past trying to build present from scratch.<br /> <br /> 7. How to define Redemption.<br /> <br /> You didn't got the theme at all. Demon isn't in it to ask if you redeem yourself according to any particular standard of redemption.<br /> <br /> It asks which standards you build. What counts as redemption, what must be done or suffered to fit the bill and clean the record.<br /> <br /> Not just for you, by the way.<br /> <br /> 8. Faith as Responsibility.<br /> <br /> Devil's Due default to Thralls and cultists as the medieval idea of Devil worshippers. They get a Torment trait as they're corrupted by you and what empowers the Pact is their decision to go ahead.<br /> <br /> In DtF the Pact is defined by faith, by intimate, confident belief in the power of a covenant, but without fixing the nature of this covenant. You define how you go for it, what you'll be for your Thrall and how you'll fit or subvert expectations and guide their future outside giving orders.<br /> <br /> 9. Overall how you choose to change the lives you touch.<br /> <br /> DtF doesn't prescribe what your powers or your presence do to people. You have potential in as many directions as possible. You're not Evil by nature, your &quot;nature&quot; is a blank slate.<br /> <br /> Your choice isn't a binary of letting Torment go forth or block it, it's an open question of which paths you see and what you choose to make of them.<br /> <br /> 10. Judge yourself and the world.<br /> <br /> Again, you're not seeking redemption unless you want. You're not at fault to begin with. You are passing judgment and all the standards are up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall DtF needs revisions, no one denied that, but it has the basic structure and narrative in a good direction. It's also open for interpretation and exploration.<br /> <br /> Your main point is the very problem with Devil's Due in all of this: feeling more &quot;demonic&quot;. This is subjective as fuck and thematically narrow. Devil's Due don't invite you to explore what you think a Fallen is or can be, it assumes a given notion of &quot;demon&quot; and roll with it, love it or leave it.<br /> <br /> It subordinates all the questions above to this conceptualization of what a demon is instead of making it one option among many, while DtF works to ask you how you conceptualize Fallen Angels and what you'll do from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: Well, you partly hit the nail on the head with the biggest problem with Demon: The Fallen. It's not about demons, it's about angels. You say that evil is tangential to the themes, and that's an inherent problem in a game called &quot;Demon: The Fallen,&quot; IMO. <br /> <br /> 2: What about the Lore system in D:tF is BETTER at embodying these themes than using Devil's Due? You keep saying &quot;Devil's Due does nothing to enforce these themes,&quot; but you haven't told me what Fallen does to enforce these themes.<br /> <br /> 3: Why is my point subjective but yours isn't? My point is that I think you can embody those themes and also make the demons feel more demonic by taking away some of their mortal certainty about their reasons for falling. I don't think them being certain they didn't do anything wrong is a major thematic flaw in the game line, and one that the game line itself struggled with.<br /> <br /> Here's my question for you: What do you think D:tF's problems are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T06:38:55-07:00","id":1561707,"title":"","content":"For context, this is how I would redo Demnon:<br /> <br /> 1: As mentioned, use the Devil's Due power system instead of Lores.<br /> <br /> 2: Add Angel player characters, using the lores from D:tF as their power system. The backstory is that, after the fall, some angels decided to stay on Earth to try and fix it, knowing that the choice would ban them from ever returning to heaven. In the milennia since then, they've devolved into different factions that ideologically disagree about how to fix the world. with the &quot;mainstream&quot; faction having a policy of no direct interference in human affairs, while the more &quot;extreme&quot; faction are an illuminati style secret society trying to bring about the apocalypse to cleanse the earth.<br /> <br /> 3: I'd give the angel factions a complicated relationship with the demon factions. The mainstream angels would have a Cold war relationship with the Faustians and a hot war relationship with the Lucifarians, while the extreme faction would recognize the Luciferians as the &quot;official&quot; opposition and exist in a Cold war with them where they actually sometimes work together to attain shared goals, while they view the other demon factions as faithless vermin.<br /> <br /> 4: I would remove the certainty about the nature of The Fall. It's been too long, and the Celestials have spent too much time melded with the minds of humans to recall with any true certainty. The official story is what most demons believe, but there's disagreement, and the angels have their own stories.<br /> <br /> 5: Everyon hates the Earthbound. That's the one thing uniting every faction, demon and angel alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T07:35:11-07:00","id":1561709,"title":"","content":"Demons are defined as fallen/former angels in this game though. And ambiguity Is one the big aspects of this game, none of what the fallen say about themselves and their history was certain anyway, between their Torment in Hell and having to have most of their celestial selves suppressed by their mortal hosts. <br /> <br /> The fallen have to determine these things for themselves now, they rejected God and now must live with its absence. I do feel like the setting of the game could fo expansion and fleshing out beyond the society of the fallen. Like more detail and guidance on the remants of the past, how demons deal/relate to the current mortal world and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T08:32:35-07:00","id":1561710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you partly hit the nail on the head with the biggest problem with Demon: The Fallen. It's not about demons, it's about angels. You say that evil is tangential to the themes, and that's an inherent problem in a game called &quot;Demon: The Fallen,&quot; IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's only so if you believe Demons and evil have to be inherently related, and fair enough that seemed to be the case on WoD when they weren't playable.<br /> <br /> However the premise of &quot;Demon: The Fallen&quot; it's different - much like how most WoD games add some layer of their own brand of moral dilemas over the identity of &quot;the monster&quot; (Werewolves being Warriors of Gaia, Mage being about philosophical conflicts)<br /> <br /> Demons are Fallen Angels with a very &quot;better to rule in hell than serve in heaven&quot; theme to them<br /> <br /> It's a story where Angels did all sort of incredibly cruel deeds in the name of God, and you can't be sure wheter God is or isn't <i>good</i>, and she ain't talking with you anyway - so you have to make your own choices.<br /> <br /> It's a game about freedom that has moral ambiguity backed on it's very essence, where you play an eldritch being trying to find it's place on a world they barely recognize.<br /> <br /> Trying to make it about good vs. evil it's basically another game. Hence why actual Angels aren't even a thing 'til the end of the world <hr /><br /> I'm not a super fan about the power system of DtF, as a list of almost static powers that then get's expanded on other supplements with rituals and whatnot. I don't think it makes a stellar job defining those themes ... but I do like the themes themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-15-2026, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T08:33:29-07:00","id":1561711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561706#post1561706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: Well, you partly hit the nail on the head with the biggest problem with Demon: The Fallen. It's not about demons, it's about angels. You say that evil is tangential to the themes, and that's an inherent problem in a game called &quot;Demon: The Fallen,&quot; IMO.<br /> <br /> 2: What about the Lore system in D:tF is BETTER at embodying these themes than using Devil's Due? You keep saying &quot;Devil's Due does nothing to enforce these themes,&quot; but you haven't told me what Fallen does to enforce these themes.<br /> <br /> 3: Why is my point subjective but yours isn't? My point is that I think you can embody those themes and also make the demons feel more demonic by taking away some of their mortal certainty about their reasons for falling. I don't think them being certain they didn't do anything wrong is a major thematic flaw in the game line, and one that the game line itself struggled with.<br /> <br /> Here's my question for you: What do you think D:tF's problems are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire was in the 90s about beings who are not completely driven to evil and instead had to manage an alien force of destruction inside in order to stay functional, while balancing needs and ambitions with human yearnings.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is about an animist society of sacred beasts that live alongside humanity despite the secrecy, supported by hidden communities of followers of an ancient religion and waging war on a lovecraftian force of corruption.<br /> <br /> Mage is about a secret war between 9 different visions of culture and philosophy and a cabal of scientists who became lost in its own needs of control over reality.<br /> <br /> You can use the first to build a vampire, the second to build a werewolf and the third to build a mage. Same goes for Wraith, Changeling, Mummy and Hunter.<br /> <br /> So, yeah: Demon is not about demons. Is about something more complex that can, if you want, be a demon. But you can explore in many other ways.<br /> <br /> It could have been different, sure. It could be based on the actual origin of the word and be about companion spirits that don't need to be evil, either.<br /> <br /> The point is precisely that this is the reason the players who like DtF don't like Devil's Due, and I don't care about you liking DD as much as you seem miffed by others liking DtF more.<br /> <br /> Not the same game. Not the same proposal. Not the same public.<br /> <br /> And the reason DD isn't conducive of an entire <u><i><b>gameline</b></i></u> is precisely the narrower scope, the fact it is exclusively for this particular view of what a demon is or can be. The reason your subjective bias is a problem here is that it ignores what other players may want. Even if DD is better at running what you want, DtF is serviceable. DD can't run a game where even a single player don't want to play your strict vision of a demon.<br /> <br /> Given that I'm not required to say why DtF is better at being DtF, since you're the one who came into a DtF discussion to argue DD is objectively better, I'll still say that the Lore system tries to convey the idea of knowledge about a facet of reality, while the Arcana of DD is a collection of independent effects.<br /> <br /> Devil's Due is already a game. It's there. It work. It is also exactly what it was made to be: a VDA supplement. It uses VDA rules and premises, it was never intended to be a full gameline. And it doesn't have to be? It's perfectly serviceable as is for its intended demographics, AFAIK. Do you feel the need for it to be something else?<br /> <br /> On my opinion of what's a problem with DtF, as most DtF players I think the Lores need a heavy revision and the system needs polish. Nothing too different from what every other line needed when they first got out, but worsened by the fact it got less dev time back in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T08:55:37-07:00","id":1561713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrere Oil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561709#post1561709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are defined as fallen/former angels in this game though. And ambiguity Is one the big aspects of this game, none of what the fallen say about themselves and their history was certain anyway, between their Torment in Hell and having to have most of their celestial selves suppressed by their mortal hosts.<br /> <br /> The fallen have to determine these things for themselves now, they rejected God and now must live with its absence. I do feel like the setting of the game could fo expansion and fleshing out beyond the society of the fallen. Like more detail and guidance on the remants of the past, how demons deal/relate to the current mortal world and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ambiguity is one of the areas where Demon: The Fallen fails the most. The book makes it very clear that the Demons are tortured good guys who were trying to save humanity when they fell. The lack of certainty you're describing is something they tried to add into later books, but the core book is extremely clear about the morality of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T08:57:07-07:00","id":1561715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561711#post1561711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point is precisely that this is the reason the players who like DtF don't like Devil's Due, and I don't care about you liking DD as much as you seem miffed by others liking DtF more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not miffed about anything. What makes you think I'm upset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T09:01:24-07:00","id":1561716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561710#post1561710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's only so if you believe Demons and evil have to be inherently related, and fair enough that seemed to be the case on WoD when they weren't playable.<br /> <br /> However the premise of &quot;Demon: The Fallen&quot; it's different - much like how most WoD games add some layer of their own brand of moral dilemas over the identity of &quot;the monster&quot; (Werewolves being Warriors of Gaia, Mage being about philosophical conflicts)<br /> <br /> Demons are Fallen Angels with a very &quot;better to rule in hell than serve in heaven&quot; theme to them<br /> <br /> It's a story where Angels did all sort of incredibly cruel deeds in the name of God, and you can't be sure wheter God is or isn't <i>good</i>, and she ain't talking with you anyway - so you have to make your own choices.<br /> <br /> It's a game about freedom that has moral ambiguity backed on it's very essence, where you play an eldritch being trying to find it's place on a world they barely recognize.<br /> <br /> Trying to make it about good vs. evil it's basically another game. Hence why actual Angels aren't even a thing 'til the end of the world <hr /><br /> I'm not a super fan about the power system of DtF, as a list of almost static powers that then get's expanded on other supplements with rituals and whatnot. I don't think it makes a stellar job defining those themes ... but I do like the themes themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>I never suggested making it about good VS evil. I'm also not saying the themes of D:tF are bad. I think you misunderstand my intentions. I want to add more ambiguity, not take ambiguity away. The problem I have with D:tF, as it exists, is that it really isn't ambiguous. The Fallen are heroes who were right to rebel. It's hard to read D:tF any other way, especially starting with the sourcebook. Adding angel player characters and making the Fallen more demonic isn't about creating a morally simple battle of good VS evil, it's about mudding those waters even more. Were the fallen right to rebel? Where the angels wrong to stay loyal? I want these questions to be actual questions that players have to try and figure out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T11:24:30-07:00","id":1561723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561716#post1561716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never suggested making it about good VS evil. I'm also not saying the themes of D:tF are bad. I think you misunderstand my intentions. I want to add more ambiguity, not take ambiguity away. The problem I have with D:tF, as it exists, is that it really isn't ambiguous. The Fallen are heroes who were right to rebel. It's hard to read D:tF any other way, especially starting with the sourcebook. Adding angel player characters and making the Fallen more demonic isn't about creating a morally simple battle of good VS evil, it's about mudding those waters even more. Were the fallen right to rebel? Where the angels wrong to stay loyal? I want these questions to be actual questions that players have to try and figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't read DtF like that, quite the opposite: a demon who derives power from Evil and Vice is quite clearly bad, even if now capable of redemption. If Angels are completely distinct entities, their nature is also set in stone, even if currently corrupting.<br /> <br /> DtF doesn't guarantee the presentation is true to any particular degree, and you seem to be completely ignoring the thousands of years of war where everyone went from goody-two-shoes to absolute assholes in both sides.<br /> <br /> Or the factions that want to use or just destroy humanity and the world.<br /> <br /> You're not muddying the waters, you're forcing demons to be a narrow definition of demon and start from there. Which is not a bad proposal, but is definitely narrower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T11:54:29-07:00","id":1561728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561723#post1561723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't read DtF like that, quite the opposite: a demon who derives power from Evil and Vice is quite clearly bad, even if now capable of redemption. If Angels are completely distinct entities, their nature is also set in stone, even if currently corrupting.<br /> <br /> DtF doesn't guarantee the presentation is true to any particular degree, and you seem to be completely ignoring the thousands of years of war where everyone went from goody-two-shoes to absolute assholes in both sides.<br /> <br /> Or the factions that want to use or just destroy humanity and the world.<br /> <br /> You're not muddying the waters, you're forcing demons to be a narrow definition of demon and start from there. Which is not a bad proposal, but is definitely narrower.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree with your framing (&quot;forcing&quot; demons to be a &quot;narrow&quot; definition definitely has a negative tone to it I don't agree with), I do agree that I am trying to get to a starting point where the player character demons feel more inherently demonic. What I disagree with is this: &quot;a demon who derives power from Evil and Vice is quite clearly bad, even if now capable of redemption.&quot; That's only true on a purely superficial level. Just because they're in that position now, doesn't mean that they deserved to be put in that position. If anything, I think it raises a lot of questions that help muddy the water a lot further. How is it just to create an entity and put it in a position where it is forced to draw strength from sin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T12:30:10-07:00","id":1561730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561715#post1561715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not miffed about anything. What makes you think I'm upset?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact you seem incapable of accepting that people simply don't share your view.<br /> <br /> Look at this conversation. From the first time you posted, people just argued that Devil's Due don't cover their vision of Demon. No one said you should change systems, no one said your take was wrong, we just said &quot;I like those other things, DtF does that for me&quot;.<br /> <br /> My very first response to you was: &quot;I think 'more demonic' is narrow, I want to explore these other concepts 'full spectrum'&quot;.<br /> <br /> You keep saying DD is superior.<br /> You keep saying 'more demonic' is better.<br /> You keep saying how DtF is inferior.<br /> You keep demanding we prove DtF worthiness.<br /> You keep refusing to engage actual arguments.<br /> <br /> You seem definitely miffed that your simplistic proposal of &quot;ditch DtF and play DD instead&quot; was met with &quot;I'm not interested in DD&quot;.<br /> <br /> No one cares you like Devil's Due more. I don't even think anyone here would refuse to play it given the opportunity. Precisely because it's a distinct proposal, I don't think you should force yourself to like DtF more or anything like that. If anything I think it's awesome that we have both Devil's Due and DtF to play.<br /> <br /> But I'd feel a lot more comfortable if you just accepted that people looking for reforming the Lores system want the Lores system and not the Arcana of Devil's Due. You completely derailed the thread with a tangent no one asked for because you can't live with DtF being a thing people like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T12:48:27-07:00","id":1561732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561730#post1561730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact you seem incapable of accepting that people simply don't share your view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I accept that. We wouldn't be having this conversation if your view wasn't different from mine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561730#post1561730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at this conversation. From the first time you posted, people just argued that Devil's Due don't cover their vision of Demon. No one said you should change systems, no one said your take was wrong, we just said &quot;I like those other things, DtF does that for me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I get that. But I wanted to understand why you thought that. Why Devil's Due doesn't work for those things isn't obvious to me, so I wanted to understand your point of view better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561730#post1561730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My very first response to you was: &quot;I think 'more demonic' is narrow, I want to explore these other concepts 'full spectrum'&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And I wanted to know why you thought 'more demonic' is more narrow, and why you thought a more demonic approach prohibited exploring these other concepts 'full spectrum,' because the why of that is not obvious to me like it is to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561730#post1561730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep saying DD is superior.<br /> You keep saying 'more demonic' is better.<br /> You keep saying how DtF is inferior.<br /> You keep demanding we prove DtF worthiness.<br /> You keep refusing to engage actual arguments.<br /> <br /> You seem definitely miffed that your simplistic proposal of &quot;ditch DtF and play DD instead&quot; was met with &quot;I'm not interested in DD&quot;.<br /> <br /> No one cares you like Devil's Due more. I don't even think anyone here would refuse to play it given the opportunity. Precisely because it's a distinct proposal, I don't think you should force yourself to like DtF more or anything like that. If anything I think it's awesome that we have both Devil's Due and DtF to play.<br /> <br /> But I'd feel a lot more comfortable if you just accepted that people looking for reforming the Lores system want the Lores system and not the Arcana of Devil's Due. You completely derailed the thread with a tangent no one asked for because you can't live with DtF being a thing people like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've completely misread my tone from the moment this conversation started. I am completely capable of living with people liking DtF.<br /> <br /> I said that I prefer to use the Devil's Due system. It was a simplistic remark, sure, but I didn't intend it to be dismissive, I was just bringing up an alternative. When you said it didn't work, I was very genuinely asking why, I wasn't upset about anything. I'm sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T12:57:40-07:00","id":1561733,"title":"","content":"Listen, I genuinely apologize. I really wasn't trying to have a fight. I'll just bow out, this isn't important anyway and I don't want to upset people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T23:53:36-07:00","id":1561809,"title":"","content":"I was giving more serious thought to the problem of the Lores after all that, and how to make a more interesting mechanic around the concept, and I arrived at two conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1. Given they're about understanding the laws underpinning reality, what if they could be used as Abilities? The core use isn't to make specific effects, but rather to understand/use the true laws of Reality? Still brewing this concept, but would love some feedback and ideas for how to execute it.<br /> <br /> 2. Changeling 20 managed to open up the Arts to have a lot more applications through the mechanic of Unleashing. Could that be used as inspiration for a similar way of expanding the uses of Lores?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T07:08:22-07:00","id":1561821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561809#post1561809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Given they're about understanding the laws underpinning reality, what if they could be used as Abilities? The core use isn't to make specific effects, but rather to understand/use the true laws of Reality? Still brewing this concept, but would love some feedback and ideas for how to execute it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like this idea.<br /> <br /> A way it's to expand their inherent perception powers. Demons can see trough all illusions, and distinguish all kinds of magic for what they are ... but that's the extent of their &quot;lore&quot; about things, barring a specific power that allows to know more.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking you could fool the &quot;demon of earth&quot; that created precious stones with a fake plastic jewel as long as it's not magicaly fake, if they don't have the purely humane knowledge in the area to not get fooled. I'm not opposed to humans fooling demons, but I do think demons should be able to &quot;know things&quot; about their specific portfolio, even if they do not perhaps use the same words to identify it. &quot;Maybe the world changed, but that's not how rocks were suppposed to work&quot;<br /> <br /> On this end, the Apocaliptic Form power of &quot;predicting weather&quot; should be scrapped and added as a baseline for anyone with the relevant Lores. I've known people to leave the game forever when they discovered that they have to spend Faith and access their all-powerfull form that scares and awes mortals simply by existing, in order to say &quot;tomorrow it's going to raaaain!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . IDK who tought it was a great idea to have that kind of power as part of the Form :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Changeling 20 managed to open up the Arts to have a lot more applications through the mechanic of Unleashing. Could that be used as inspiration for a similar way of expanding the uses of Lores? </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad idea, but it would need to be thematically different. Lores it's a wordplay because it's knowledge, but it's also that demons are the <i>Lords</i> of Creation. They're not an expression of another world that's alive and has an agenda. Their powers aren't something that can be &quot;unleashed&quot;, as such.<br /> <br /> More likely, it's like their Apocaliptic Form, a manifestation of themselves on reality. It could be tainted by their Torment, but that's the extent of it's chaoticness. Magic ain't going to do &quot;as it wills&quot;, it's going to do as <i>they </i>will, if a bit twisted (or a lot if they're too far gone, but at that point that's sort of their their will too - most of the time) <hr />One solution I've vouched for these problems in the past it's to use Lores as Spheres, using the power on each level as an example of what could be done on each level - this solves both issues because Spheres have an in built &quot;knowledge function&quot; on their first level, and they're open ended.<br /> <br /> And Demon does compare the powers of mages with their own saying they're basically Lores, <i>except</i> it also says humans can &quot;reinvent&quot; the Lores (guess it's the privilege of being &quot;made in the image of God&quot;), so <i>maybe that's too much freedom</i>. <hr /><br /> One very common &quot;demonic pact&quot; it's to produce gold and jewels from earth to make someone rich. You can interpret a pact to raise Resources as that. But Demons can't do that for themselves. Only trough pacts can they do this sort of stuff - and this is backed in the lore. Humans <i>allow</i> demons to rewrite reality with their Faith, it's what they have now that they don't have God backing them.<br /> <br /> Now, leaving aside how pacts are very restrictive themselves as a system (being limited by both the faith of humans being very low, and the system not allowing enough freedom to the point it requires another book with a list of powers to do some classic demonic pacts, like longevity), as an idea to expand the system w/o making it just open ended we could try to use the pacts as more than just a battery.<br /> <br /> Like, for option 1), you could use Pacts as a way to access Backgrounds, perhaps more than the ones allowed for Thralls, and maybe other Traits such as Merits &amp; Defects, even powers from other splats (if sorcerers can, why not?). <i>At a cost</i> for the pact (and for the thrall). Like, you could invoke stone golems as Allies, impose a Defect as a curse, and speak to animals. That + Lores acting like Abilities could provide a flexible system.<br /> <br /> For option 2) Could be a way to to <i>limit </i>or <i>access </i>the expansion of Lores, trough Unleashing or whatever. So you don't depend on making the effect too wild or too <i>personaly</i> costly to explain why the secondary system isn't used <i>all </i>the time - it is still something you have to build up.<br /> <br /> One of many peeves I have about Demon it's how the &quot;weapon&quot; Faustians want to make it's never ever defined or even suggested of how could it matter at all. Faith it's just &quot;blood for vampires&quot; - there's 0 purpose of having more faith sources than what you need to be &quot;filled&quot;, and the power of thralls doesn't impress enough as to consider Pacts as such an absolute Game Changer. Demons don't even <i>have</i> any power that could matter in such a war - how do you even <i>find</i> Heaven?, how do you <i>affect</i> it?. All you get it's to be able to cast your five-per-tree Lores a lot.<br /> <br /> Mastery it's more impressive, and it's not Pact dependant. Rituals are more interesting, and they're dependant on working in concert more than massive quantities of Faith.<br /> <br /> Yet Faith it's important enough that Demons immediately lost the war when humans saw them for the monsters they were, and the &quot;faith flow&quot; stopped. I don't feel this importance it's sufficently sustained by the idea that they were unable to &quot;cast&quot; as much as they would have wanted.<br /> <br /> But if freely given human faith regulates the mojo then it makes more sense. Suddenly Demons were &quot;demoted&quot; from free Dynamic Magic to maybe Static Magic - that has to hurt ... and On Game, to imagine Faith as a &quot;weapon&quot; that could change the game it's less of an outlandish idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe even allow a limited access to Mastery at some (very high) amount of Pacts, to add <i>punch </i>to the versatility - and suddenly Faustians oppening a hole in Heaven doesn't sound <i>so </i>far fetched\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T00:33:37-07:00","id":1561962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561821#post1561821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like this idea.<br /> <br /> A way it's to expand their inherent perception powers. Demons can see trough all illusions, and distinguish all kinds of magic for what they are ... but that's the extent of their &quot;lore&quot; about things, barring a specific power that allows to know more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not a bad idea, but it would need to be thematically different. Lores it's a wordplay because it's knowledge, but it's also that demons are the <i>Lords</i> of Creation. They're not an expression of another world that's alive and has an agenda. Their powers aren't something that can be &quot;unleashed&quot;, as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have something to work with here.<br /> <br /> So, my thoughts for now, but I'll need time to revise some rules in several books:<br /> <br /> 1. The Lores are applied through a number of distinct mechanics, as Knowledge, Awareness, &quot;Unleashing&quot;, Arcana (the specific powers, borrowing the name from DD), Revelation (I'm thinking on redesigning the rules for Apocalyptic Forms and also refine those for collecting Faith) and Pactiser (borrowing from French, inspiration from another thread).<br /> <br /> 2. Knowledge and Awareness are the baseline mechanic: a Fallen can roll Lores as they roll any Ability, but the information they can glean is preternatural. Each Lore will have examples, but include things like knowing all the weather patterns of the world in any age and sensing the weather well enough to predict a week ahead at least.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Unleashing&quot; is a placeholder name. In C20 this rule gives them a way of treating Arts as if they were Spheres, delivering a freeform magic system without just repeating the mechanics of Mage. I agree it needs changes, but the idea is the same, with more control. A means to use a Lore roll similar to an Ability that encodes in a single roll the flexibility of freeform magic and the risk of Torment.<br /> <br /> 4. Arcana would be static powers associated with the Lore. Here I'm thinking about using the V5 Discipline system: you have simpler powers, but they're several and you chose what to slot in. They'd have all powers of a given level, but &quot;slotting&quot; the power requires Faith Points and a roll.<br /> <br /> 5. Revelation would be the roll to manifest the Fallen as an avatar of the Lore. It won't define stats for the Form, but how fast and impressive it is. It may be subtle, giving off sensations that cause awe even if there's almost no visible change. That way deciding when a target has faith in the Demon isn't too subjective anymore, it's always a Revelation Roll and, with success, taking Apocalyptic Form even if &quot;subtle&quot; (as in not Masquerade breaking, but definitely quite noticeable).<br /> <br /> 6. Pactiser is the one I'm on the fence. I'm not sure if I want Lores to affect Pacts too much. I do think they need more weight, but I interpret that while the Fallen channel the power to make things happen, much of the changes the Faith cause come from the target themselves. But I can see a point in Lore use as a means to stylize Thralls for each Demon.<br /> <br /> 7. Faith cost will be an important aspect of the uses. Knowledge/Awareness has no cost and no reliance on remaining Faith, the Fallen are always capable of it. Pactiser uses the Faith of the target already, so while it requires available Faith, it doesn't cost any. Arcana are above all energy savers, using them should be cheap, but changing would be costlier. Revelation will depend on the final mechanics, and Unleashing is the most expensive of the bunch.<br /> <br /> 8. Pacts need more oomph, but that would first come from revising how much points we get to design the changes to the target. I think the base rules are serviceable: you can take up to half as toll, round down, use the rest to invest in them, and from afar Ravage them for extra dice. What we need is alternatives to channel this Faith, a way to build devices and ritual matrices that store and use this Faith, and/or the Ravaging. We also need rules for changing Faith over time.<br /> <br /> 9. Just to be clear: I'm on favor of supernatural splats being able to make Pacts by default. It's ridiculous to block when this is already a thing in their own games. What happens to them in their society is another problem.<br /> <br /> 10. Suggestion name for the project: Demon the Fallen 25th Anniversary Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T07:57:24-07:00","id":1561972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561962#post1561962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Pactiser is the one I'm on the fence. I'm not sure if I want Lores to affect Pacts too much. I do think they need more weight, but I interpret that while the Fallen channel the power to make things happen, much of the changes the Faith cause come from the target themselves. But I can see a point in Lore use as a means to stylize Thralls for each Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could leave the system open ended, but give some cost reduction if it matches the nature of the demon (as expressed by Lores) and another one if it matches the nature of the thrall (as expressed by some sort of &quot;ressonance&quot;, that could be related to Nature and maybe some elements or narratives we want to incentivize as part of the Pact). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. Just to be clear: I'm on favor of supernatural splats being able to make Pacts by default. It's ridiculous to block when this is already a thing in their own games. What happens to them in their society is another problem. </div> </div> </div>Likewise.<br /> <br /> However, I fell Demon does this not by accident, but because it wants the players to interact with human dramas more - and given how pacts work, it wouldn't be hard to imagine on crossover having the Demon just pacting with the their superfriends and leaving frail humans alone. Save maybe to have a &quot;respawn&quot; (depending on how possesing supers work)<br /> <br /> But I fell that if making many pacts it's important enough, and if they're flavorfull enough, then it wouldn't be necessary to incentivize talking to humans more - even on crossover.<br /> <br /> Maybe one could give - erm - &quot;blank state&quot; humans some extra bonus, tho. 2x1 offer on your first interaction with the supernatural, or something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . But I don't think it would be necessary if pacts are interesting enough on their own, and interesting in a way that you would want to make more than a few on the long run.<br /> <br /> The other crossover elephant in the room it's True Faith - that Demon doesn't aknowledge as existing, afaik. Tho it's easy to rule as just adding to Faith Potential","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-20-2026, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T19:55:35-07:00","id":1561985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561972#post1561972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you could leave the system open ended, but give some cost reduction if it matches the nature of the demon (as expressed by Lores) and another one if it matches the nature of the thrall (as expressed by some sort of &quot;ressonance&quot;, that could be related to Nature and maybe some elements or narratives we want to incentivize as part of the Pact).</div> </div> </div> </div>What about this:<br /> <br /> A Pact is divided in 4 parts: Desire, Demand, Accord and Fine Letters. This is less a change and more a formalization of how it already works.<br /> <br /> Desire is what the target wants, the intention. A Demon is free to favor the letter or the spirit of a Pact, but effects granted in accordance with Desire cost less.<br /> <br /> Demand is what the demon asks back and the target agrees, and Accord is any detail they negotiate to smooth things. They have no cost reduction, but the power of pure Faith gives the Fallen the ability to grant any effect that fulfills the Pact.<br /> <br /> Until here the key is: you can make anything if the target knows you're going to do something roughly in that line.<br /> <br /> Fine Letters are the changes you can add just because the target bared their soul to you and you can mess around. Those extras are limited only to not cause a break of the Pact, and they use your Lores as base.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561972#post1561972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I fell Demon does this not by accident, but because it wants the players to interact with human dramas more - and given how pacts work, it wouldn't be hard to imagine on crossover having the Demon just pacting with the their superfriends and leaving frail humans alone. Save maybe to have a &quot;respawn&quot; (depending on how possesing supers work)</div> </div> </div> </div>Other games have rules for infernalism where getting benefits through Pacts still costs XP. It is just a matter of keeping that: splats have to pay XP for Pact benefits. If you want to more freely empower your Thralls, then you need mortals.<br /> <br /> Even because splats may need custom options as they may demand other kinds of powers. A Fallen can concede infernal Rotes, teach Gifts, impart Dark Thaumaturgy. But they also live in societies where they're more vulnerable to get caught and executed. Dealing with splats is too different to be just worse or better, of changes a lot of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1560926-demon-the-fallen-lores-discussion?p=1561972#post1561972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other crossover elephant in the room it's True Faith - that Demon doesn't aknowledge as existing, afaik. Tho it's easy to rule as just adding to Faith Potential</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say True Faith starts at Faith 4/5. It isn't just greater Faith, it's Faith under certain demands, at least the requisites for the Merit. And from their, despite the name of talks more about the dedication of the character than their faith.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: Faith 4 is a prerequisite to buy True Faith, Faith 5 is a prerequisite to raise it. True Faith is not the same as Faith, but it can be added to Faith for some effects.<br /> <br /> Beware: True Faith is both demanding and very powerful. The Pact itself must be done in a way that preserves the True Faith, and breaking it will make the Thrall lose the trait, not redirect to the Fallen. This Thrall also has more defense against the Demon than most, and the ability to hurt the Demon by default.<br /> <br /> What would we want out of True Faith? Should a Thrall like that give off more points? Less? Receive more powers? None? Just roll it with rituals like Summoning or Warding? Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}